WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.150
Control automation runs one loop everywhere:
test the setting, spot the drift,

2
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.055
raise a task against the asset,
fix it on the native platform,

3
00:00:09.055 --> 00:00:12.163
and close it only when a
re-test confirms the fix.

4
00:00:12.163 --> 00:00:16.828
The cloud tools already test most
settings; your job is to own the result,

5
00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:20.387
and the coordination platform
reads but never writes.

6
00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.849
The platforms differ in ways that matter.

7
00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:26.323
Some integrations aren't
available in Azure Government,

8
00:00:26.323 --> 00:00:29.426
one AWS compliance service
is in maintenance mode,

9
00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:33.637
and on your own VMware estate the
evidence is entirely yours to build.

10
00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:37.867
The decision for the CISO: keep
the platform's identity read-only,

11
00:00:37.867 --> 00:00:40.138
with every automated fix approved.

12
00:00:40.138 --> 00:00:41.690
Next, who runs it.
